From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:43:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/44] minimize: keep Firefox matches across tab switches,
 forget counts whose source is gone

A Firefox window keeps the session window it took last while one of the
file's windows still has a page with its title, picking the one most like
it. A tab switch the file does not show yet keeps the window's own count,
and same-title windows told apart once stay apart across file updates.

A remembered count is forgotten 3 s after its source stops listing the
window: no terminal or Files file has its title (shared titles still
count as listed), or a Firefox session file written after the window took
its title has no page with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

